Building ucsd-psystem-os
========================

The p-System is built by the top-level Makefile of the UCSD-P-System
repository; see README.md there.  `make os` compiles these sources with
the freshly built cross tools (ucsd-psystem-xc) and packs them into disk
volumes with the file system tools (ucsd-psystem-fs):

    build/system.vol      the system disk
    build/utility.vol     utility programs
    build/diagnostic.vol  diagnostic disk

`make run` boots system.vol in the VM (ucsd-psystem-vm).

Peter Miller's original build instructions (Cook, autoconf) are kept, for
history, in etc/BUILDING.man.
